The legal texts are New Zealand legislation, as published in the official consolidations of the
Parliamentary Counsel Office on the New Zealand Legislation website (www.legislation.govt.nz):

  "Under section 27 of the Copyright Act 1994, there is no copyright in New Zealand legislation,
  including in legislation published by the PCO on this website."

  All other content on that website is Crown copyright, licensed under a Creative Commons
  Attribution licence (CC BY). Source: New Zealand Legislation, Parliamentary Counsel Office,
  www.legislation.govt.nz (https://www.legislation.govt.nz/copyright/).

The pages were read from Internet Archive captures (web.archive.org), whose capture timestamps are
recorded in corpus data and REPRODUCE.md.

The arrangement of this repository, its tables, commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and may be
reused under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This repository is not legal advice and not an
official publication.
